<article class="env-lemma" id="0CZ8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CZ8">Lemma <span data-tag="0CZ8">71.5.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a finite type, quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $r \geq 0$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is finite locally free of rank $r$ 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\text{Fit}_{r - 1}(\mathcal{F}) = 0$ and $\text{Fit}_ r(\mathcal{F}) = \mathcal{O}_ X$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\text{Fit}_ k(\mathcal{F}) = 0$ for $k < r$ and $\text{Fit}_ k(\mathcal{F}) = \mathcal{O}_ X$ for $k \geq r$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Reduces to Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C3G" data-tag="0C3G">31.9.5</a> by étale localization. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>